[brief] Recent work from 2024-2026 that the tools returned is mostly about production mechanisms rather than new X-ray datasets. The main papers revisit Shi-Fuller resonant production with large lepton asymme
**Survey** — 39 tools on 3 servers, 6 read-only probes, 9 papers found.

Recent work from 2024-2026 that the tools returned is mostly about production mechanisms rather than new X-ray datasets. The main papers revisit Shi-Fuller resonant production with large lepton asymmetries. Vogel, Garcia Escudero, Froustey and Abazajian (arXiv:2507.18752) find that asymmetries L >~ 0.5 at T > 20 MeV are consistent with BBN and CMB, and that they open a viable region at m_s >~ 10 keV and sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-14. That region is compatible with NuSTAR and INTEGRAL/SPI X-ray limits and with Lyman-alpha inferences of a thermal-equivalent WDM mass m_th ~ 4.1 keV. Gorbunov, Kalashnikov and Krugan (arXiv:2502.17374) show that flavor-dependent asymmetries, which work best with inverted ordering, can cancel the BBN limits on mixing and give colder spectra, which reopens lighter masses at smaller mixing. Two other papers extend the picture but were seen only as abstract snippets: a 2026 paper on cold sterile-neutrino DM from inflaton decays during reheating (arXiv:2601.03346) and a 2026 paper on lepton asymmetry saturating resonant production (arXiv:2609.31340). The overall picture is that standard non-resonant (Dodelson-Widrow) production is excluded by X-ray limits combined with structure formation. What survives sits at very small mixing, roughly sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-11 to 1e-14 depending on mass, and needs either resonant production with BBN-compatible lepton asymmetry or a non-oscillation mechanism such as reheating or scalar decays. A web snippet (not citable; no arXiv ID found) says eROSITA eFEDS line searches over 1.8-18 keV, and eROSITA diffuse limits more broadly, are now the strongest in their band. Warning: I had no sterile-neutrino BBN tool for Yp or D/H, so none of the BBN statements here are numbers I computed. They come only from paper abstracts and still need to be checked by calculation.

Quantities worth checking: Radiative decay rate Gamma = 1.38e-32 s^-1 (sin^2 2theta / 1e-10) (m_s / keV)^5 and the line energy E = m_s/2, to convert X-ray flux limits into sin^2(2theta) limits; Shift in Yp from Delta N_eff and from a nu_e asymmetry xi_e (roughly dYp/dxi_e ~ -0.25), checked against the measured Yp ~ 0.245 +/- 0.003; D/H as a function of Delta N_eff and eta_b, checked against (2.53 +/- 0.03) x 1e-5; Lepton asymmetry L(m_s, sin^2 2theta) needed for Omega_s h^2 = 0.12 under Shi-Fuller production, compared with the BBN-allowed |xi_e| <~ 0.03 at T < 1 MeV and larger L above 20 MeV; Thermal-equivalent WDM mass m_th for each point, compared with Lyman-alpha bounds (m_th >~ 4-6 keV); Dodelson-Widrow abundance Omega_s h^2 ~ 0.1 (sin^2 2theta / 3e-9)(m_s / 3 keV)^1.8, to confirm that pure non-resonant production is excluded.
