**Finding:** 2507.18752 (full text) states: L >~ 0.5 at high T opens viable space at m_s >~ 10 keV and sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-14; structure bounds used are m_th > 8.4 keV (galaxy counts, 95% CL), m_th > 8.5 keV (counts + strong lensing), and a Lyman-alpha preference m_th = 4.1 (+33.3/-1.5) keV; NuSTAR gives sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-12 for 6-40 keV and INTEGRAL/SPI gives sin^2(2theta) <~ 3e-14 for m_s >~ 40 keV (lifetimes < ~1e20 s excluded).
