[tool] d-03 post_finding {"claim": "Mechanism map (from literature quotes, not computed by tools). Shi-Fuller resonant production with L >~ 0.5 above 20 MeV is viable at m_s >~ 10 keV a
[finding] f-004 Mechanism map (from literature quotes, not computed by tools). Shi-Fuller resonant production with L >~ 0.5 above 20 MeV is viable at m_s >~ 10 keV and sin^2(2t
**Finding:** Mechanism map (from literature quotes, not computed by tools). Shi-Fuller resonant production with L >~ 0.5 above 20 MeV is viable at m_s >~ 10 keV and sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-14 (2507.18752). Its X-ray ceilings are NuSTAR sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-12 at 6-40 keV and SPI <~ 3e-14 above 40 keV. Its structure-formation bounds are m_th > 8.4-8.5 keV (galaxy counts and lensing) or the Lyman-alpha preference m_th ~ 4.1 keV. Flavor-dependent asymmetries, which work best with inverted ordering, open lower mixing angles and give colder spectra that reopen lighter m_s (2502.17374, abstract only). Large L saturates resonant production, which leaves about a two-decade window in sin^2(2theta) (2609.31340, abstract only). Inflaton-decay reheating production with BR <~ 1e-4 gives cold DM at mixings below the X-ray limits, which oscillation production cannot populate (2601.03346, abstract only).
