**Finding:** The server's radiative decay rate agrees with Gamma = 1.38e-32 s^-1 (sin^2 2theta/1e-10)(m_s/keV)^5 to within about 1.5%. At m_s = 7.1 keV and sin^2 2theta = 1e-10 the tool gives 2.46e-28 s^-1 (formula 2.49e-28) with E_line = 3.55 keV. At 20 keV and 1e-12 it gives 4.36e-28 s^-1 (formula 4.42e-28) with E_line = 10 keV. The tool's built-in X-ray limits (NuSTAR M31, Roach+2020; XMM blank sky, Dessert+2020) exclude both points.
