[finding] f-006 DW benchmark grid (m_s = 7.1, 10, 20, 50 keV; sin^2 2theta = 1e-10, 1e-12, 1e-14): no point is BBN-excluded (Delta N_eff <= 2.9e-3, |Delta chi^2| <= 0.04). DW O
**Finding:** DW benchmark grid (m_s = 7.1, 10, 20, 50 keV; sin^2 2theta = 1e-10, 1e-12, 1e-14): no point is BBN-excluded (Delta N_eff <= 2.9e-3, |Delta chi^2| <= 0.04). DW Omega_s h^2 reaches 0.12 only near sin^2 2theta ~ 1e-10 at m_s ~ 10-20 keV (0.087 at 10 keV; 0.30 at 20 keV, which overcloses), and 50 keV at 1e-10 gives 1.58. At X-ray-allowed mixings of 1e-12 to 1e-14, DW gives Omega_s h^2 <= 0.016, so a non-DW mechanism is needed.
