**Completed — Survey the 2024-2026 production-mechanism literature (Shi-Fuller resonant production with lepton asymmetry, reheating production, scalar decays) and test its viability claims against tool-computed BBN numbers, adding the Lyman-alpha and structure-formation bounds..** All four arXiv IDs resolve to real papers (f-001): 2507.18752 (Vogel et al. 2025), 2502.17374 (Gorbunov, Kalashnikov and Krugan 2025), 2601.03346 (Cline and Xu 2026) and 2609.31340 (Gorbunov and Kalashnikov 2026). So 2609.31340 is genuine and q-03 is answered. I read the full text of 2507.18752, cited it in runs/261021_110150/references.bib and saved the text as runs/261021_110150/2507.18752.txt (f-002). The paper's viable region is m_s >~ 10 keV and sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-14 for L >~ 0.5 at T > 20 MeV. Its bounds: NuSTAR sin^2(2theta) <~ 1e-12 at 6-40 keV, INTEGRAL/SPI <~ 3e-14 above 40 keV, m_th > 8.4 keV from galaxy counts, m_th > 8.5 keV from counts plus lensing, and a Lyman-alpha preference m_th = 4.1 (+33.3/-1.5) keV. Tool tests (f-003; CSVs sterile_nu_grid_SF_fdf543.csv and sterile_nu_grid_SF_d81486.csv) at m_s = 10, 20 and 30 keV with sin^2(2theta) = 1e-14 in SF mode give Delta N_eff ~ 1e-8 and BBN Delta chi^2 = 0 (allowed). At 20 keV Yp = 0.24682 and D/H = 2.4433e-5. Omega_s h^2 is 0.122, 0.490 and 1.10 at L = 1e-3 and ten times larger at L = 0.1; all of these points are flagged as overclosing. The tool cannot test the paper's claims. Its L is capped at 0.1 while the paper needs L >~ 0.5. Its SF Delta N_eff is a heuristic (0.1 x the DW value). It does not feed a xi_e effect into Yp, so the |xi_e| <~ 0.03 condition cannot be checked. Its SF Omega_s h^2 is not a Boltzmann calculation, so the overclosure flag does not contradict the paper. The BBN 'allowed' verdict is trivially true rather than supporting evidence. The server uses Yp = 0.2449 +/- 0.004 and D/H = 2.547 +/- 0.025 (relevant to q-02). Mechanism map (f-004) from the 2502.17374, 2609.31340 and 2601.03346 abstracts only: flavor-dependent asymmetries reopen lighter masses and smaller mixings; large L saturates resonant production, leaving about a two-decade window in sin^2(2theta); inflaton-decay reheating production with BR <~ 1e-4 populates cold DM below the X-ray limits. The survey criteria are only partly met. The full text of 2502.17374 was not read, so its viable ranges have no verbatim quotes. The 2024+ structure-formation search found only arXiv:2409.18917 (mixed WDM from Milky Way satellites), which was neither read nor cited. Open question q-07 asks for a BBN code that accepts xi_e, which a real test would need.
