**Finding:** XRISM Resolve stacked 3.75 Ms of data on ten galaxy clusters (arXiv:2510.24560, 2025) and found no unidentified lines over 2.5-15 keV. Its 3-sigma upper limit on the decay rate of an m_s ~ 7.1 keV particle (E = 3.55 keV) is Gamma ~ 1.0e-27 s^-1. That is 3-4 times stronger than the Hitomi Perseus limit but still 5 times above the rate implied by the Bulbul+2014 XMM detection, so XRISM does not yet rule out the 3.55 keV line. Scaling the server's rate (2.46e-28 s^-1 at sin^2 2theta = 1e-10) gives sin^2 2theta < ~4e-10 at 7.1 keV from XRISM alone.
