**Completed — Quantify the X-ray decay-line constraints. Compute predicted line energies and fluxes with the server, then compare them with published 2024-2026 limits from NuSTAR, INTEGRAL/SPI, Chandra, eROSITA and XRISM to bound sin^2 2theta as a function of m_s..** Partly done: the decay-rate check and the 3.55 keV line status are complete, but the table of X-ray limits versus mass is not. (1) Decay-rate check (f-005; tc-...-25, tc-...-27): the server's rate matches Gamma = 1.38e-32 s^-1 (sin^2 2theta/1e-10)(m_s/keV)^5 to within about 1.5%. At m_s = 7.1 keV and sin^2 2theta = 1e-10 the tool gives 2.46e-28 s^-1 (formula 2.49e-28), with E = 3.55 keV and lifetime 4.07e27 s. At 20 keV and 1e-12 it gives 4.36e-28 s^-1 (formula 4.42e-28), with E = 10 keV. The rate normalisation in arXiv:2405.17861 Eq. 2 (1.36e-32 s^-1 at sin^2 2theta = 1e-10 and 1 keV) falls in the same range. Whole-halo fluxes at 7.1 keV and 1e-10 are 4.68 ph/s/cm^2 for the Milky Way centre, 6.89e-4 for M31 and 3.55e-5 for Perseus (f_DM = 1, no field-of-view cut). The tool's built-in NuSTAR M31 (Roach+2020) and XMM blank-sky (Dessert+2020) limits exclude both test points. (2) DW benchmark grid at 4 masses x 3 mixings (f-006; CSV /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-sterile-bbn-xray/runs/261021_110150/sterile_nu_grid_DW_5199ae.csv): no point is BBN-excluded (Delta N_eff <= 2.9e-3). Omega_s h^2 is 0.087 at 10 keV and 1e-10, 0.30 at 20 keV and 1e-10 (overcloses), and 1.58 at 50 keV and 1e-10 (overcloses). At mixings of 1e-12 to 1e-14, Omega_s h^2 <= 0.016, so a non-DW mechanism is needed. Only the 1e-10 mixing was run through the X-ray tool at 7.1 keV, and only 1e-12 at 20 keV. (3) Status of the 3.55 keV line (f-012, cited in references.bib under key arxiv251024560): XRISM Resolve stacked ten clusters for 3.75 Ms (arXiv:2510.24560) and found no unidentified lines. Its 3-sigma limit is Gamma ~ 1.0e-27 s^-1 at m_s ~ 7.1 keV, 3-4 times stronger than Hitomi but still 5 times above the Bulbul+2014 XMM signal, so the line is constrained but not ruled out. Scaling the tool's rate turns this into sin^2 2theta < ~4e-10. (4) NuSTAR 11-year stray-light limits (arXiv:2405.17861, Fig. 3, 95% CL, m_s ~ 6-40 keV; f-013) reach the lower edge of resonant-production predictions, but the numbers at 7, 10 and 20 keV were not read off the figure. Open items: the table of sin^2 2theta limits at 7, 10, 20 and 50 keV has no figure-read values yet (q-08). Searches for 2024-2026 eROSITA and INTEGRAL/SPI limits found nothing (dead end x-01). The XRISM-derived limit at 7.1 keV is the only quoted entry; 10, 20 and 50 keV need Fig. 3 of 2405.17861 and an SPI or NuSTAR GC source. The NuSTAR paper was not added to the bib.
