**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 9 findings stand up to the evidence, 4 questioned ('2507.18752 (full text) states: L >~ 0.5 at high T opens viable space at m_s >~ 10 keV and ': The quoted evidence is a download confirmation (tc-...-30) and characters 0-9000 of the paper (tc-...-37), which show only the title, authors and affiliations. None of the claimed numbers appear in the quoted excerpts: L >~ 0.5, m_s >~ 10 keV, sin^2 2theta <~ 1e-14, m_th > 8.4/8.5 keV, m_th = 4.1 (+33.3/-1.5) keV, NuSTAR 1e-12, SPI 3e-14. They may appear later in the 62k-character file, but the cited excerpts do not contain them.; 'Mechanism map (from literature quotes, not computed by tools). Shi-Fuller resonant product': The 2507.18752 numbers depend on the unevidenced f-002. Several specifics are not in the truncated abstracts quoted: the inverted-ordering preference and 'colder spectra' for 2502.17374, and the 'about two-decade window in sin^2 2theta' for 2609.31340. tc-...-51 is a pre-2024 review listing and supports none of these details.; 'XRISM Resolve stacked 3.75 Ms of data on ten galaxy clusters (arXiv:2510.24560, 2025) and ': tc-...-61 is an affiliations chunk (characters 9000-14000) and tc-...-62 is only a citation confirmation. Neither contains the 3.75 Ms exposure, the 2.5-15 keV band, Gamma ~ 1.0e-27 s^-1, the comparison with Hitomi or the comparison with Bulbul+2014. Only the final scaling (1e-27 / 2.46e-28 = 4.1, giving about 4e-10) can be checked, and it is correct given those inputs.; 'Krivonos, Barinov, Mukhin and Gorbunov (arXiv:2405.17861, 2024) use 11 years of NuSTAR str': The excerpts (title page and methods text on CXB fitting) do not contain Eq. 2, the Fig. 3 axis range or the 'bottom edge of theoretical predictions' quote. The claim also has an arithmetic inconsistency. The server's rate implies a coefficient of 2.46e-28 / (7.1^5 x 1e-10) = 1.36e-32, so the paper's 1.36e-32 matches the server to within about 0.3% rather than sitting 1% above it. The quoted '1.36e-22' also mis-transcribes the exponent.).

Issues: The DW normalization ambiguity decides the DW verdict at 7.1 keV. The server's DM line is at 2.55e-10. The brief's formula gives about 7.6e-10. The XRISM-only limit is about 4e-10. So DW at 3.5 keV is allowed under one normalization and excluded under the other. Neither normalization has been checked against a published DW production calculation, including its QCD-era uncertainty.; The SM D/H baseline (2.4433e-5) is 2.9 sigma below the brief's value and about 4 sigma below the server's 2.547 +/- 0.025. Because exclusion uses Delta chi^2 relative to the SM, extra radiation partly improves the D/H fit. This is why 1 keV at 3e-7 (Yp at +2.3 sigma) has Delta chi^2 of only 0.44. The Delta N_eff < 0.548 bound is therefore sensitive to the nuclear-rate choice and the baseline. This does not change the DW conclusion, but it matters for resonant-production claims.; The core deliverable, sin^2 2theta limits as a function of m_s, is missing at 10, 20 and 50 keV. NuSTAR Fig. 3 values were not read. No INTEGRAL/SPI or eROSITA 2024-2026 limit was sourced. The only number entering the viability table relies on the unevidenced f-002, so the viable region cannot yet be stated quantitatively from verified sources..
