**Next steps after wave 1** — One wave and 23 tool calls remain, so the plan uses two focused directions of about 11 calls each rather than three. I close d-04 because a synthesis run before verification would only restate the contested numbers. Its table becomes the final step of the first direction, which first re-supports f-002, f-012 and f-013 with verbatim quotes and fills the missing X-ray limits at 10-50 keV, the critic's top issue. The second direction resolves the DW normalization ambiguity, which decides the 7.1 keV verdict, and adds m_th along the DW line so the structure-formation exclusion is actually quantified. The critic's BBN-robustness suggestion is folded into the second direction as a short analytic check rather than run as a separate direction, to stay within budget. The tools cannot test resonant production at L >~ 0.5, so those claims stay literature-sourced and are labelled that way. The task does not require a facility run, so none is scheduled.

New lines of investigation: Re-extract the quantitative literature claims (f-002, f-012, f-013) as verbatim quotes. Build a verified X-ray limit table at m_s = 7.1, 10, 20, 40 and 50 keV. Then produce the final per-mechanism viability table in the (m_s, sin^2 2theta) plane (DW, Shi-Fuller with lepton asymmetry, flavor-dependent asymmetry, reheating production), with a provenance column for each entry.; Settle the factor-3 DW relic-density normalization against a published calculation and compute m_th along the DW dark-matter line. Also give a short BBN robustness check: the Delta N_eff bound under the brief's data versus the server's data, and the joint (Delta N_eff, xi_e) bound using dYp/dxi_e ~ -0.25..
