**Finding:** f-012 re-supported verbatim from XRISM 2510.24560 abstract: "We stack 3.75 Megaseconds of early XRISM Resolve observations of ten galaxy clusters to search for unidentified spectral lines in the E= 2.5-15 keV band (rest frame)... No unidentified lines are detected... with the 3σ upper limit on the m_s∼7.1 keV DM particle decay rate (which corresponds to a E= 3.55 keV emission line) of Γ∼1.0×10^-27 s^-1. This upper limit is 3−4 times lower than the one derived by Hitomi ... but still 5 times higher than the XMM-Newton detection reported by Bulbul et al. (2014)". With Γ = 1.38e-32 (sin^2 2θ/1e-10)(m_s/keV)^5 s^-1 this converts to sin^2 2θ < ~4e-10 at 7.1 keV (3σ, cluster J-factors as in the paper; derived, not quoted).
