[finding] f-016 f-013 partially re-supported, but the requested figure readings were not obtained. Verbatim from 2405.17861: Eq. 2 reads "Γγ = 9/1024 α/π^4 G_F^2 m_s^5 sin^2 2θ
**Finding:** f-013 partially re-supported, but the requested figure readings were not obtained. Verbatim from 2405.17861: Eq. 2 reads "Γγ = 9/1024 α/π^4 G_F^2 m_s^5 sin^2 2θ = 1.36×10^-22 (m_s/1keV)^5 sin^2 2θ s^-1". The exponent -22 is correct as written, because sin^2 2θ is not normalized there; it equals 1.36e-32 s^-1 at sin^2 2θ = 1e-10, so the board's "correction to 1e-32" applies only to the normalized form. The paper places "new upper limits on the active-sterile mixing angle θ for sterile neutrino masses m_s = 6−40 keV" at 95% CL. Fig. 3 is plotted on a sin^2(2θ) axis from 1e-15 to 1e-10. The paper says that observed limits are "stronger ... in certain mass ranges (e.g. m_νs = 8−9 keV or 23−25 keV)", and that "the borderline excess at 40 keV is the known instrumental effect". I could not read numerical values at 7, 10 or 20 keV: Fig. 3 is missing from the HTML rendering, and the Fig. 1 image (registered as Figure 15) was downloaded but cannot be digitized with the available tools. So the only NuSTAR number per mass is the secondary 2507.18752 summary, sin^2 2θ <~ 1e-12 across 6-40 keV.
