[finding] f-019 The published DW normalization (Abazajian 2017 review, arXiv:1705.01837 Eq. 37, a fit from Ref. [120]) is m_s ~ 3.40 keV (sin^2 2theta/1e-8)^-0.615 (Omega_DM/0.
**Finding:** The published DW normalization (Abazajian 2017 review, arXiv:1705.01837 Eq. 37, a fit from Ref. [120]) is m_s ~ 3.40 keV (sin^2 2theta/1e-8)^-0.615 (Omega_DM/0.26)^0.5 x 0.527 erfc[-1.15 (T_QCD/170 MeV)^2.15]. Inverting it gives a DM line at sin^2 2theta ~ 1.23e-8 (3 keV), 3.0e-9 (7.1 keV), 1.73e-9 (10 keV), 5.6e-10 (20 keV) and 1.26e-10 (50 keV). The server line from the tool is 1.2e-9, 2.55e-10, 1.37e-10, 3.9e-11 and 7.6e-12 (Omega_s h^2 = 0.119-0.120). So the published line needs 10x (3 keV) to 17x (50 keV) more mixing than the server and 3.4-5.5x more than the brief's formula. The two differ in shape as well as normalization: Omega is proportional to m^2 (sin^2 2theta)^1.23 rather than m^1.8 times sin^2 2theta.
[tool] tc-261021_1-w2-d-06-102 -> ok: Recorded finding f-019.
