**Completed — Settle the factor-3 DW relic-density normalization against a published calculation and compute m_th along the DW dark-matter line. Also give a short BBN robustness check: the Delta N_eff bound under the brief's data versus the server's data, and the joint (Delta N_eff, xi_e) bound using dYp/dxi_e ~ -0.25..** Normalization (f-019): the published DW fit in arXiv:1705.01837 (Abazajian review) Eq. 37 is m_s ~ 3.40 keV (sin^2 2theta/1e-8)^-0.615 (Omega_DM/0.26)^0.5 x 0.527 erfc[-1.15 (T_QCD/170 MeV)^2.15]. It is cited in references.bib under key arxiv170501837. I inverted it by hand. Its dark-matter line sits at sin^2 2theta ~ 1.23e-8 (3 keV), 3.0e-9 (7.1 keV), 1.73e-9 (10 keV), 5.6e-10 (20 keV) and 1.26e-10 (50 keV). The QCD-era uncertainty (T_QCD 150-200 MeV) moves these by about +10%/-7%. The server line from predict_sterile_nu_grid (sterile_nu_grid_DW_2461e9.csv, Omega h^2 = 0.119-0.120) is 1.2e-9, 2.55e-10, 1.37e-10, 3.9e-11 and 7.6e-12. The published normalization therefore needs 10-17x more mixing than the server and 3.4-5.5x more than the brief's formula, and it scales differently with mass and mixing. Verdict at 7.1 keV (f-020): against the XRISM limit of about 4e-10, the server line (2.55e-10) survives, while the brief's line (7.65e-10) and the published line (3.0e-9) are excluded. Using the published normalization, DW at 7.1 keV is excluded by about 7.5x. m_th (f-021): I used the DW-to-thermal mapping m_s = 4.43 keV (m_th)^(4/3) from Viel+2005 (astro-ph/0501562). I downloaded that paper but did not quote the coefficient verbatim from it. This gives m_th = 0.75, 1.42, 1.84, 3.10 and 6.16 keV at m_s = 3, 7.1, 10, 20 and 50 keV. Lyman-alpha (m_th > 4-6 keV) then needs m_s > 28-48 keV, and satellite counts (m_th > 8.4 keV) need m_s > 76 keV. At those masses the DW line under any of the three normalizations sits well above the NuSTAR (~1e-12) and SPI (~3e-14) ceilings, so the surviving DW mass interval is empty. BBN (f-022): these are analytic results from linearized f-009 slopes, not server runs. Upper bounds on Delta N_eff at 95%, relative to the SM: with the brief's data, 0.32 from Yp only, 0.58 from D/H only and 0.47 combined. With the server's data, 0.46, 0.66 and 0.61. The server tool itself quotes 0.548. The SM D/H sits 2.9-4.1 sigma low, so D/H prefers Delta N_eff ~ 0.3 and the bound moves by 0.1-0.2 depending on the baseline. For the joint bound I used dYp/dxi_e = -0.25 and 2-dof Delta chi^2 < 5.99. Brief data: Delta N_eff in [0.04, 0.48], with xi_e = 0.0073 + 0.054 Delta N_eff +/- 0.029. Server data: Delta N_eff in [0.13, 0.50], with xi_e = 0.0077 + 0.054 Delta N_eff +/- 0.039. Overall |xi_e| <~ 0.03-0.06. Question q-09 is posted. Open items: the Viel coefficient and the full Eq. 37 citation still need verbatim quotes, and dD/H/dxi_e was neglected.
